/**
 * @page installation Installation Guide
 *
 * @section install_prereq Prerequisites
 * Before installing ArgusAI, ensure you have the following prerequisites:
 * - Python 3.8 or higher
 * - Node.js 16 or higher
 * - Git
 * - CUDA-capable GPU (recommended)
 *
 * @section install_backend Backend Installation
 * 1. Clone the repository:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    git clone https://github.com/yourusername/ArgusAI.git
 *    cd ArgusAI
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 2. Create and activate a virtual environment:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    python -m venv venv
 *    source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 3. Install backend dependencies:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    cd backend
 *    pip install -r requirements.txt
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 4. Download YOLO models:
 *    - yolov8n.pt
 *    - yolov8n-seg.pt
 *    - yolov8l.pt
 *
 * @section install_frontend Frontend Installation
 * 1. Navigate to the frontend directory:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    cd ../frontend
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 2. Install frontend dependencies:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    npm install
 *    @endcode
 *
 * @section install_config Configuration
 * 1. Backend configuration:
 *    - Copy `.env.example` to `.env`
 *    - Update configuration values as needed
 *
 * 2. Frontend configuration:
 *    - Copy `.env.example` to `.env`
 *    - Update API endpoints and other settings
 *
 * @section install_run Running the Application
 * 1. Start the backend server:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    cd backend
 *    uvicorn main:app --reload
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 2. Start the frontend development server:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    cd frontend
 *    npm run dev
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 3. Access the application:
 *    - Frontend: http://localhost:5173
 *    - Backend API: http://localhost:8000
 *    - API Documentation: http://localhost:8000/docs
 *
 * @section install_trouble Troubleshooting
 * Common issues and solutions:
 * - CUDA errors: Ensure CUDA is properly installed and compatible with PyTorch
 * - Port conflicts: Change ports in configuration files
 * - Model loading errors: Verify model files are in the correct location
 * - Dependencies issues: Update pip and npm to latest versions
 *
 * @section install_update Updating
 * To update the application:
 * 1. Pull latest changes:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    git pull origin main
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 2. Update dependencies:
 *    @code{.bash}
 *    # Backend
 *    cd backend
 *    pip install -r requirements.txt
 *
 *    # Frontend
 *    cd ../frontend
 *    npm install
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 3. Restart the application
 */ 